    "created_at": "2022-02-01T12:21:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-01T12:21:14Z",
    "body": "I don't see anything semantically wrong with this change. However, I think it's in general not particularly beneficial to tweak the states, since it causes review churn to compare implementations with the spec. Also, there is always a chance for bugs with supposed no-op changes.\r\n\r\nTo the extent implementations don't try to manually inline across these transitions, which would put more distance between what the code looks like and what the spec looks like, it seems to me that this ends up with more branches executed in the common case even if it results in less code. That is, the current character gets checked for being `>` more times in the case where the tag ends.\r\n\r\nI'm not strongly against this change, but I'm also not convinced that it's a useful change.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
